R"VG(
# news5.vg (H-04's second pass): the everyday in the news's register, continued: a law, a trial, envoys, a disaster at the works, a price,
# a new play or song, the ruler's visit.

# ---- a law ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.law
  {news.h.law}\n{news.law.m} {news.law.x}
news.h.law
  A new law
  The new law
  ($e.what=tax) A new tax
  ($e.what=curfew) Curfew
  ($e.what=census) The count of the people
news.law.m
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:full} has decreed that {news.law.what}.
  It is decreed at {$seat} that {news.law.what}.
  From the first of {season.next}, {news.law.what}.
  The law passed this week says, in short, that {news.law.what}.
news.law.what
  ($e.what=measures) every measure in the land is to be the measure of {city}, and the old ones broken
  ($e.what=tax) every house is to pay {n} {coin} a year on its {news.law.taxed}
  ($e.what=water) the water of {river} is to be shared by turns, each district its day
  ($e.what=tolls) the tolls on the bridges are doubled, to pay for the bridges
  ($e.what=curfew) nobody is to be in the streets after the last bell without a lamp and a reason
  ($e.what=coin) the old {coin} are to be called in and new ones struck, with a new head on them
  ($e.what=inheritance) a house is to pass to the eldest child, whoever that may be
  ($e.what=drink) no {drink} is to be sold on the rest day, nor on the day before
  ($e.what=weapons) no weapon is to be carried within the walls but a kitchen knife
  ($e.what=school) every child is to be taught to read until the age of {n}
  ($e.what=census) every house is to be counted, its people and their trades
  ($e.what=calendar) the year is to begin at {festival} and not in {season.any}
  ($e.what=dogs) every dog is to have a collar and an owner willing to say so
  ($e.what=hours) no hand is to work more than {n} hours a day, the owners objecting
  ($e.what=noise) no {instrument} is to be played after midnight within the town
  ($e.what=forests) the {tree} of the state forests are not to be cut without a licence
  ($e.what=rations) bread, salt and {fuel} are to be had by ticket only
news.law.taxed
  windows
  doors
  hearths
  {herd}
news.law.x
  The {ind.trade.p} are said to be furious.
  {news.said} that the law was long overdue.
  Nobody at {$home} has read it through yet except the {ind.trade.p}, who read nothing else.
  It will be enforced, {news.said}, gently at first.
  The fine for breaking it is {n} {coin}, or a day in the stocks by {holyplace}.
ind.trade.p
  innkeepers
  carters
  bakers
  farmers
  shopkeepers
  publicans

# ---- a trial ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.trial
  {news.h.trial}\n{news.trial.m} {news.trial.v}
news.h.trial
  The trial at {$e.place}
  ($e.verdict=acquitted) Acquitted
  ($e.verdict=condemned) Guilty
  (has:$e.a) The case of {$e.a:name}
news.trial.m
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:full} was tried at {$e.place} this week for {news.trial.what}.
  (has:$e.a has:$e.a.trade) {$e.a:full}, {$e.a.trade}, stood trial at {$e.place} on a charge of {news.trial.what}.
  (!has:$e.a) A man of {$e.place} whose name the court has withheld was tried for {news.trial.what}.
  The trial at {$e.place} for {news.trial.what} ended yesterday after {n} days, and the courtroom was full every one of them.
news.trial.what
  ($e.what=theft) theft from {holyplace}
  ($e.what=murder) the murder of a neighbour
  ($e.what=treason) treason against {ruler.the}
  ($e.what=heresy) heresy against the faith of {god}
  ($e.what=forgery) forging the {coin} of the realm
  ($e.what=fraud) fraud against the {craft} guild
  ($e.what=smuggling) smuggling {drink} over the border
  ($e.what=bribery) bribing the market inspectors
  ($e.what=arson) setting fire to a neighbour's {crop}
  ($e.what=libel) libel, against the editor of a rival paper
news.trial.v
  ($e.verdict=acquitted) The jury acquitted, and the crowd outside cheered, or most of it did.
  ($e.verdict=acquitted) The verdict was not guilty, and the accused walked out into {town.open} a free {news.trial.who}.
  ($e.verdict=condemned) The verdict was guilty; the sentence will be given on the rest day.
  ($e.verdict=condemned) Found guilty, the prisoner said nothing at all.
  ($e.verdict=exiled) The court has sent the prisoner over the border, never to return on pain of death.
  ($e.verdict=fined) The court fined the prisoner {n} {coin}, which was paid at once, in small coin, from a bag.
news.trial.who
  person
  citizen
  neighbour

# ---- envoys --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.embassy
  ($e.what=city has:$e.place2) Envoys at {$e.place}\nEnvoys from {$e.place2} arrived at {$e.place} this week {news.emb.why}. {news.emb.x}
  ($e.what=others) The {other} send envoys\nEnvoys of the {other} have come to {$e.place} {news.emb.why}. {news.emb.x}
  ($e.what=sent) Our envoys go to the {other}\nEnvoys have left {$e.place} for the country of the {other}, {news.emb.sent}. {news.emb.x}
news.emb.why
  to talk about the tolls
  with gifts and a long list of complaints
  to settle the matter of the border fields
  to ask for help against the floods
  for reasons nobody will tell this paper
news.emb.sent
  carrying gifts of {craft} and a letter nobody has been allowed to read
  to talk about trade and, it is hoped, about nothing else
  with {herd} as gifts, and a guard
news.emb.x
  (has:$e.a) The envoy, {$e.a:full}, is said to be a patient {news.emb.man}.
  They were given dinner at {hall}, and the dinner was long.
  The talks will go on until {season.next}.
  Their dress was much admired in {town.open}.
news.emb.man
  speaker
  listener
  negotiator

# ---- a disaster at the works -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.accident
  {news.h.acci}\n{news.acci.m} {news.acci.x}
news.h.acci
  Disaster at {$e.place}
  ($e.what=mine) The mine at {$e.place}
  ($e.what=bridge) The bridge falls
  ($e.what=ship) Ship lost
  ($e.what=train) Railway accident
  ($e.what=explosion) Explosion at {$e.place}
  ($e.what=dam) The dam breaks
news.acci.m
  ($e.what=bridge) The bridge at {$e.place} gave way under a loaded cart [at noon|in the dusk|on market day], and {#$e.value} went into the river with it.
  ($e.what=mine) The roof of the mine at {$e.place} came down {news.acci.when}; {#$e.value} men are dead and the digging goes on {news.acci.dig}.
  ($e.what=ship) The {news.acci.ship} went down off {$e.place} in the gale with {#$e.value} aboard; {n} were saved.
  ($e.what=train) The night train came off the rails near {$e.place}; {#$e.value} are dead and many more hurt.
  ($e.what=explosion) An explosion at the works at {$e.place} was heard ten miles away; {#$e.value} are dead.
  ($e.what=explosion) The {craft} works at {$e.place} blew up {news.acci.when}, killing {#$e.value} and breaking every window in {streets.of}.
  ($e.what=dam) The dam above {$e.place} broke {news.acci.when}, and the water took {#$e.value} with it, and the {crop} of the valley.
  ($e.what=aircraft) An aircraft fell on the edge of {$e.place}; all {#$e.value} aboard are dead.
  ($e.what=reactor) The reactor at {$e.place} has failed; {#$e.value} are dead, and the town is being emptied.
  ($e.what=habitat) The habitat at {$e.place} was breached; {#$e.value} are dead.
  ($e.what=tower) A tower being built at {$e.place} fell into the street, killing {#$e.value}.
  ($e.what=well) The shaft of a new well at {$e.place} collapsed on the diggers; {#$e.value} are dead.
news.acci.ship
  ferry from {city}
  {crop} boat
  packet boat
  fishing fleet's biggest boat
news.acci.x
  The families are waiting at the gate for news, with {food} and blankets.
  An inquiry has been promised, and so has compensation, in that order, in {coin}.
  The owners say everything was done according to the rules, and the rules are being looked at by {news.lookers}.
  A fund for the families has been opened, and the {craft} guild has given {nbig} {coin}.
  The bells of {$home} will be rung for them on the rest day, and the dead buried at {deadplace}.

# ---- a price ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.price
  {news.h.price}\n{news.price.m} {news.price.x}
news.h.price
  ($e.out=1) Prices rise
  ($e.out=0) Prices fall
  The price of {news.price.what}
news.price.m
  ($e.out=1) The price of {news.price.what} has risen {news.price.by} {season.this}, {news.price.why.up}.
  ($e.out=0) The price of {news.price.what} has fallen {news.price.by} {season.this}, {news.price.why.down}.
  ($e.out=1) {news.price.What} is dearer by {#$e.value} in the hundred, and the {news.price.who} say it will go higher.
  ($e.out=0) {news.price.What} is cheaper by {#$e.value} in the hundred, and nobody can say for how long.
news.price.what
  ($e.what=bread) bread
  ($e.what=salt) salt
  ($e.what=oil) lamp oil
  ($e.what=rent) rooms in the town
  ($e.what=cloth) cloth
  ($e.what=meat) meat
  ($e.what=fuel) {fuel}
  ($e.what=water) water
news.price.What
  ($e.what=bread) Bread
  ($e.what=salt) Salt
  ($e.what=oil) Lamp oil
  ($e.what=rent) Rent
  ($e.what=cloth) Cloth
  ($e.what=meat) Meat
  ($e.what=fuel) {fuel}
  ($e.what=water) Water
news.price.by
  ($e.value<15) a little
  ($e.value>=15 $e.value<35) by a quarter
  ($e.value>=35) by half
news.price.why.up
  the harvest having been poor
  the carters having raised their charges
  for no reason anyone will give
  the {craft} trade buying everything it can
news.price.why.down
  the harvest having been good
  the new road bringing it in from the hills
  the traders having overbought
news.price.who
  bakers
  shopkeepers
  dealers
news.price.x
  The poor of {$home} will feel it first.
  The council is asked to fix the price, and has said it will think about it.
  A loaf at {$home} costs {n} {smallcoin}.
  The women of the market have their own views, which this paper cannot print.

# ---- a show ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.show
  {news.h.show}\n{news.show.m} {news.show.x}
news.h.show
  At the theatre
  A new {news.show.what}
  ($e.what=pictures|$e.what=statue) The exhibition
news.show.m
  (has:$e.a) A new {news.show.what} by {$e.a:full} was given at {$e.place} this week, and {news.show.how}.
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:full}'s {news.show.what} has been the talk of {$e.place}; {news.show.how}.
  The new {news.show.what} at {$e.place} {news.show.how}.
news.show.what
  ($e.what=play) play
  ($e.what=song) song
  ($e.what=pictures) pictures
  ($e.what=film) film
  ($e.what=dance) dance
  ($e.what=poem) poem
  ($e.what=statue) statue
news.show.how
  the hall was full every night
  the critics hated it and the audience did not
  half the audience left and the other half stood
  nobody can agree what it means, which is said to be the point
  the {festival} songs will never sound the same
news.show.x
  It will be given again at {festival}.
  Tickets are {n} {smallcoin}, and worth it, this paper thinks.
  The council has asked to see it first, and then asked to see it again.
  There is a song in it about {river} that the whole town is already whistling.

# ---- a visit -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.visit
  (has:$e.a) {news.h.visit}\n{$e.a:full} came to {$e.place} this week, {news.visit.how}. {news.visit.x}
news.h.visit
  A visit
  {$e.a:name} at {$e.place}
  A royal day
news.visit.how
  and was met at the gate by the whole council and most of the town
  without warning, which caught the council in its shirtsleeves
  to open the new hall, which was not finished
  to hear the town's complaints, all of them
news.visit.x
  The streets were swept for the first time since {festival}.
  The children were given a holiday and {food}.
  The visit lasted a day; the cost will last longer.
  (has:$e.place.landmark) A tour of {$e.place.landmark} was given, and admired.
  A {colour.holy} carpet was laid from the gate to {hall}, and the {herd} were kept out of the way.
news.acci.when
  in the night shift
  at the change of shifts
  {time.of}
  on the day before {festival}
news.acci.dig
  by lamplight
  with picks and bare hands
  without rest
  in shifts of {n}
news.lookers
  the council
  the guild of the {craft} trade
  a committee of the owners
  anyone with the time
)VG"
